  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sornavel vs State Represented Through on 12 January, 2024 Author: R.Hemalatha Bench: R.Hemalatha Crl OP(MD)No.289 Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated : 12.01.2024 Coram The Honourable Mrs.Justice R.Hemalatha CRL.O.P(MD)No.2892 of 2021 and Crl.M.P(MD)Nos.1561 and 1562 of 2021 Sornavel ... Petition Vs State Represented through The Food Safety Officer, Code No.412, Dindigul Town, Corporation Siddha Hospital, Nagal Nagar, Dindigul-624003. ... Respondent Prayer: Criminal Original Petition filed under Section 482 of the C Criminal Procedure to call for the records in connection with the impugned Charge Sheet in C.C.No.449 of 2020 on the file of the lear Judicial Magistrate No.III, Dindigul, Dindigul District and quash t same insofar as the petitioner is concerned. 1/4 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis Crl Op( Sornavel vs State Represented Through on 12 January, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/19588409/ 1 For Petitioner : Ms.S.Gokila Santhiya for Mr.S.Sarvagan Prabhu For Respondent : Mr.R.M.Anbunithi Additional Public Prosecut Order",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "2. Mr.R.M.Anbunithi, learned Additional Public Prosecutor appearing for the respondent, on instructions, would contend that bailable warrant is pending against the present petitioner and since the petitioner did not appear before the concerned Magistrate Court, he cannot maintain the present petition. 3. In view of the above, the petitioner is directed to appear before the learned Judicial Magistrate No.III, Dindigul, within a period of two weeks from the date of receipt of a copy of this order, failing which, the learned Judicial Magistrate shall take corecive steps to secure the https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis presence of the petitioner."
  },
